  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# 3.15.0.1\n\nFirst release on [dd-sdk-ios 3.15.0](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-sdk-ios/releases/tag/3.15.0),\nbuilt from source for Mac Catalyst. Package ids, namespaces and the version scheme are\nunchanged; the fourth component is this repository's binding revision, starting again at 1 on\nthe new native line.\n\n## What's new upstream\n\nMost of 3.15.0 lands somewhere a Catalyst app can use it, but not all of it:\n\n- **The UK1 datacenter is now reachable** — `DDSite.Uk1()`. This is the one change with a\n  managed API attached; see below.\n- **KSCrash is bumped to 2.5.1** inside `DatadogCrashReporting`, which is the crash reporter\n  these packages actually use.\n- **WebView tracing no longer drops early requests.** Upstream's `onSessionStart` now fires only\n  once the sampling information WebView Tracking depends on is in place, and WebView RUM `ddtags`\n  are merged by key rather than repeated. Both reach `DatadogNet.WebViewTracking.Mac` consumers.\n- **Session Replay capture fidelity** — visual effects, embedded content and gradients — is the\n  bulk of the release upstream and **changes nothing here**. `DatadogNet.SessionReplay.Mac` links\n  and records nothing on Catalyst, as the package table in the README says; the improvement is\n  real on iOS and inert on this platform.\n- A Swift-6-only crash fix for `onSessionStart` is not reachable from C# at all. It ships in the\n  same binaries.\n\nUpstream's own notes are the reference:\n[3.14.0…3.15.0](https://github.com/DataDog/dd-sdk-ios/compare/3.14.0...3.15.0).\n\n## Binding changes\n\nOne member, arriving through the usual re-sync from\n[DatadogNet.iOS](https://github.com/sbokatuk/DatadogNet.iOS) — the binding sources here are\nverbatim copies of that repository's, and CI enforces it:\n\n```csharp\nvar configuration = new DDConfiguration(clientToken: \"<CLIENT_TOKEN>\", env: \"production\")\n{\n    Site = DDSite.Uk1(),\n};\n```\n\n`DDSite` is a class of static factory methods, so it is `DDSite.Uk1()`, not a constant. The full\nset is now `Us1()`, `Us3()`, `Us5()`, `Eu1()`, `Ap1()`, `Ap2()`, `Uk1()`, `Us1_fed()`,\n`Us2_fed()`. Nothing else in the managed surface moved: the header diff upstream reports one\nchanged framework and one added line in it.\n\n`OpenTelemetryApi` stays on the release 3.14.0 pinned — 3.15.0's `Cartfile.resolved` names the\nsame one — so `DatadogNet.OpenTelemetryApi.Mac` is a rebuild rather than an upgrade.\n\n## Upgrading from 3.14.0.x\n\n```diff\n-<PackageReference Include=\"DatadogNet.RUM.Mac\" Version=\"3.14.0.4\" />\n+<PackageReference Include=\"DatadogNet.RUM.Mac\" Version=\"3.15.0.1\" />\n```\n\nNothing else to change. No type moved, nothing was removed or renamed, and the package set is the\nsame; all packages move together as they depend on each other at an exact version.",
